1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,526
EVA: Arch Linux, its own Wayland desktop. Meet the beta.

2
00:00:05,277 --> 00:00:09,236
Find apps and files, or switch to the Orbit launcher.

3
00:00:09,986 --> 00:00:14,363
Prisma brings previews, tabs and everyday file operations
together.

4
00:00:15,113 --> 00:00:17,981
Super B gathers your open apps in one shelf.

5
00:00:18,731 --> 00:00:22,504
Tab shows your windows and virtual desktops at a glance.

6
00:00:23,254 --> 00:00:26,900
Snap organizes your windows with six ready-made layouts.

7
00:00:27,650 --> 00:00:31,539
Explore the cover library. These games are demonstration
entries.

8
00:00:32,289 --> 00:00:35,064
Pick your backgrounds by workspace and monitor.

9
00:00:35,814 --> 00:00:39,587
Video wallpapers work too. This animation comes from NASA.

10
00:00:40,337 --> 00:00:43,205
Add clocks, notes and other widgets to your desktop.

11
00:00:43,955 --> 00:00:47,682
Change colors and switch between light and dark
appearance.

12
00:00:48,432 --> 00:00:52,937
Drag bar modules into place. EVA manages the available
space.

13
00:00:53,687 --> 00:00:57,379
Edit shortcuts and use the keyboard layout you choose.

14
00:00:58,129 --> 00:01:01,136
Keep events and reminders in your local calendar.

15
00:01:01,887 --> 00:01:05,602
Check live system usage and available hardware sensors.

16
00:01:06,352 --> 00:01:09,452
Control compatible players without leaving the desktop.

17
00:01:10,202 --> 00:01:13,499
Care for a desktop companion and visit its habitat.

18
00:01:14,249 --> 00:01:17,442
Connect the AI island to your own compatible provider.

19
00:01:18,193 --> 00:01:20,759
Choose a boot theme visually in Settings.

20
00:01:21,510 --> 00:01:26,560
EVA beta. Your desktop, your rhythm. Download for x86
sixty-four.
